# Tests — DATA-RET R-3 retention periods and R-6 backup bound

Assertion-based tests for `Retention.RetentionEnd`. All six limbs of the
R-3.1 table are covered, both limb-specific exceptions are covered on both
sides, and the month-end cases where Catala date addition would raise are
tested explicitly.

Three families of test exist specifically to catch encoding defects the type
checker cannot see:

* **R-3.1(d) is a maximum over two dates.** `MarketingCollectionLater`
  supplies an engagement date *earlier* than the collection date, so an
  encoding that ran the 24 months from either date unconditionally would give
  the wrong answer on one of that pair of tests.
* **Trap 1, exceptions not inheriting their parent's condition.**
  `ConsentIgnoredForEmployeeRecord` puts a talent-pool consent date on an
  Employee Record and `StatutoryIgnoredForCustomerContract` turns the
  statutory determination on for a Customer Contract. An exception written
  without its own limb condition would fire in both and change the answer.
* **Month-end rounding.** `EmployeeRecordMonthEnd` (6 years from 29
  February) and `SecurityLogMonthEnd` (13 months from 31 January) are the
  cases where `|2020-02-29| + 6 year` and `|2025-01-31| + 13 month` are
  ambiguous. The scope declares `date round down`, so both land on 28
  February.

`statutory_retention_period` is `0 day` wherever `statutory_retention_applies`
is false: the input must still be supplied, and no limb reads it.

> Using Retention

## R3_1_a_EmployeeRecord

R-3.1(a): 6 years from the end of employment. R-6.1 then adds the 90-day
backup bound.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_1_a_EmployeeRecord:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_1_a_EmployeeRecord:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.EmployeeRecord
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2019-08-31|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Absent
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Absent
      -- consent_renewal_dates: []
      -- statutory_retention_applies: false
      -- statutory_retention_period: 0 day
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2025-08-31|
  assertion r.backup_purge_deadline = |2025-11-29|
```

## R3_1_a_EmployeeRecordMonthEnd

6 years from 29 February. `|2020-02-29| + 6 year` has no corresponding day
and would raise; `date round down` resolves it to 28 February 2026.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_1_a_EmployeeRecordMonthEnd:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_1_a_EmployeeRecordMonthEnd:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.EmployeeRecord
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2020-02-29|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Absent
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Absent
      -- consent_renewal_dates: []
      -- statutory_retention_applies: false
      -- statutory_retention_period: 0 day
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2026-02-28|
  assertion r.backup_purge_deadline = |2026-05-29|
```

## R3_1_b_CustomerContract

R-3.1(b): 7 years from expiry or termination of the contract.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_1_b_CustomerContract:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_1_b_CustomerContract:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.CustomerContract
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2018-03-15|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Absent
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Absent
      -- consent_renewal_dates: []
      -- statutory_retention_applies: false
      -- statutory_retention_period: 0 day
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2025-03-15|
```

## R3_1_c_FinancialRecord

R-3.1(c): 7 years from the end of the financial year to which it relates.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_1_c_FinancialRecord:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_1_c_FinancialRecord:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.FinancialRecord
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2020-12-31|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Absent
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Absent
      -- consent_renewal_dates: []
      -- statutory_retention_applies: false
      -- statutory_retention_period: 0 day
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2027-12-31|
```

## R3_1_d_MarketingEngagementLater

R-3.1(d): 24 months from the later of collection and most recent engagement.
Here the engagement is later, so the period runs from it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_1_d_MarketingEngagementLater:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_1_d_MarketingEngagementLater:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.MarketingContact
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2023-05-10|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Present content |2024-11-20|
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Absent
      -- consent_renewal_dates: []
      -- statutory_retention_applies: false
      -- statutory_retention_period: 0 day
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2026-11-20|
  assertion r.backup_purge_deadline = |2027-02-18|
```

## R3_1_d_MarketingCollectionLater

The other half of the "later of". The engagement predates collection, so the
period runs from collection. An encoding that took the engagement date
whenever one was present would give 2025-06-01 here.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_1_d_MarketingCollectionLater:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_1_d_MarketingCollectionLater:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.MarketingContact
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2024-01-15|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Present content |2023-06-01|
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Absent
      -- consent_renewal_dates: []
      -- statutory_retention_applies: false
      -- statutory_retention_period: 0 day
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2026-01-15|
```

## R3_1_d_MarketingNoEngagement

A contact who has never engaged: the later of the two dates is the only one
there is.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_1_d_MarketingNoEngagement:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_1_d_MarketingNoEngagement:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.MarketingContact
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2024-01-15|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Absent
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Absent
      -- consent_renewal_dates: []
      -- statutory_retention_applies: false
      -- statutory_retention_period: 0 day
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2026-01-15|
```

## R3_1_e_SecurityLog

R-3.1(e): 13 months from the logged event.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_1_e_SecurityLog:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_1_e_SecurityLog:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.SecurityLog
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2025-06-15|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Absent
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Absent
      -- consent_renewal_dates: []
      -- statutory_retention_applies: false
      -- statutory_retention_period: 0 day
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2026-07-15|
```

## R3_1_e_SecurityLogMonthEnd

13 months from 31 January lands in a month with no 31st. `date round down`
resolves it to 28 February 2026; rounding up would give 1 March and retain
the log a day longer than the Standard's maximum.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_1_e_SecurityLogMonthEnd:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_1_e_SecurityLogMonthEnd:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.SecurityLog
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2025-01-31|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Absent
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Absent
      -- consent_renewal_dates: []
      -- statutory_retention_applies: false
      -- statutory_retention_period: 0 day
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2026-02-28|
```

## R3_1_f_CandidateRecordNoConsent

R-3.1(f): 12 months from the conclusion of the recruitment process, where the
candidate has given no talent-pool consent.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_1_f_CandidateRecordNoConsent:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_1_f_CandidateRecordNoConsent:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.CandidateRecord
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2025-03-31|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Absent
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Absent
      -- consent_renewal_dates: []
      -- statutory_retention_applies: false
      -- statutory_retention_period: 0 day
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2026-03-31|
```

## R3_1_f_RenewalsWithoutConsent

A renewal register entry with no recorded consent does not engage R-3.2,
which requires that the candidate "has given consent". The R-3.1(f) period
stands.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_1_f_RenewalsWithoutConsent:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_1_f_RenewalsWithoutConsent:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.CandidateRecord
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2025-03-31|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Absent
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Absent
      -- consent_renewal_dates: [|2026-09-01|]
      -- statutory_retention_applies: false
      -- statutory_retention_period: 0 day
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2026-03-31|
```

## R3_2_TalentPoolConsentNoRenewal

R-3.2 displaces R-3.1(f): 24 months from the date of consent. Note that this
is measured from the consent date and not from the recruitment trigger, so
the answer is not 2027-03-31.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_2_TalentPoolConsentNoRenewal:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_2_TalentPoolConsentNoRenewal:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.CandidateRecord
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2025-03-31|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Absent
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Present content |2025-02-28|
      -- consent_renewal_dates: []
      -- statutory_retention_applies: false
      -- statutory_retention_period: 0 day
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2027-02-28|
```

## R3_2_TalentPoolPeriodRestartsOnRenewal

"The period restarts on each renewal of consent": the 24 months run from the
most recent renewal, 2025-08-31, and not from the original consent, which
would have given 2026-08-31.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_2_TalentPoolPeriodRestartsOnRenewal:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_2_TalentPoolPeriodRestartsOnRenewal:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.CandidateRecord
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2024-06-30|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Absent
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Present content |2024-08-31|
      -- consent_renewal_dates: [|2025-01-31|; |2025-08-31|]
      -- statutory_retention_applies: false
      -- statutory_retention_period: 0 day
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2027-08-31|
```

## R3_2_RenewalsEarlierThanConsent

A renewal register that holds only entries predating the consent cannot pull
the period backwards: the period runs from the latest of consent and renewals.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_2_RenewalsEarlierThanConsent:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_2_RenewalsEarlierThanConsent:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.CandidateRecord
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2024-06-30|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Absent
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Present content |2025-06-30|
      -- consent_renewal_dates: [|2024-01-01|]
      -- statutory_retention_applies: false
      -- statutory_retention_period: 0 day
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2027-06-30|
```

## R3_2_ConsentIgnoredForEmployeeRecord

Trap 1. R-3.2 is an exception to R-3.1(f) alone, so a talent-pool consent
date on an Employee Record must leave the 6-year period untouched. An
exception written without `data_class with pattern CandidateRecord` would
give 2027-02-28 here.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_2_ConsentIgnoredForEmployeeRecord:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_2_ConsentIgnoredForEmployeeRecord:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.EmployeeRecord
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2019-08-31|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Absent
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Present content |2025-02-28|
      -- consent_renewal_dates: []
      -- statutory_retention_applies: false
      -- statutory_retention_period: 0 day
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2025-08-31|
```

## R3_3_StatutoryPeriodLonger

R-3.3 displaces R-3.1(a) where pensions or payroll legislation requires
longer. Ten years from the end of employment beats six.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_3_StatutoryPeriodLonger:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_3_StatutoryPeriodLonger:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.EmployeeRecord
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2019-08-31|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Absent
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Absent
      -- consent_renewal_dates: []
      -- statutory_retention_applies: true
      -- statutory_retention_period: 10 year
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2029-08-31|
  assertion r.backup_purge_deadline = |2029-11-29|
```

## R3_3_StatutoryPeriodShorter

R-3.3 bites only where the statutory period is the longer one, so a shorter
statutory period cannot cut R-3.1(a) down: the result is the later of the two.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_3_StatutoryPeriodShorter:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_3_StatutoryPeriodShorter:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.EmployeeRecord
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2019-08-31|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Absent
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Absent
      -- consent_renewal_dates: []
      -- statutory_retention_applies: true
      -- statutory_retention_period: 3 year
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2025-08-31|
```

## R3_3_StatutoryPeriodEqual

The threshold itself: a statutory period of exactly six years leaves the
R-3.1(a) date unchanged.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_3_StatutoryPeriodEqual:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_3_StatutoryPeriodEqual:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.EmployeeRecord
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2019-08-31|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Absent
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Absent
      -- consent_renewal_dates: []
      -- statutory_retention_applies: true
      -- statutory_retention_period: 6 year
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2025-08-31|
```

## R3_3_StatutoryIgnoredForCustomerContract

Trap 1. R-3.3 is an exception to R-3.1(a) alone, so a standing determination
that payroll legislation requires ten years must not lengthen a Customer
Contract. An exception written without `data_class with pattern
EmployeeRecord` would give 2028-03-15 here.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_3_StatutoryIgnoredForCustomerContract:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_3_StatutoryIgnoredForCustomerContract:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.CustomerContract
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2018-03-15|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Absent
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Absent
      -- consent_renewal_dates: []
      -- statutory_retention_applies: true
      -- statutory_retention_period: 10 year
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2025-03-15|
```

## R3_3_StatutoryIgnoredForCandidateRecordWithConsent

The two limb-specific exceptions do not interfere: a Candidate Record with
talent-pool consent takes R-3.2's 24 months even though the statutory
determination is also on, because R-3.3 attaches only to limb (a).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR3_3_StatutoryIgnoredForCandidateRecordWithConsent:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR3_3_StatutoryIgnoredForCandidateRecordWithConsent:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.CandidateRecord
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2024-06-30|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Absent
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Present content |2025-06-30|
      -- consent_renewal_dates: []
      -- statutory_retention_applies: true
      -- statutory_retention_period: 10 year
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2027-06-30|
```

## R6_1_BackupBoundOnShortestPeriod

R-6.1 bounds the backup purge at 90 days after production deletion, whatever
limb fixed the production date.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestR6_1_BackupBoundOnShortestPeriod:
  output r content Retention.RetentionEnd

scope TestR6_1_BackupBoundOnShortestPeriod:
  definition r equals
    output of Retention.RetentionEnd with {
      -- data_class: Retention.DataClass.SecurityLog
      -- retention_trigger_date: |2025-01-31|
      -- most_recent_engagement_date: Absent
      -- talent_pool_consent_date: Absent
      -- consent_renewal_dates: []
      -- statutory_retention_applies: false
      -- statutory_retention_period: 0 day
    }
  assertion r.retention_end_date = |2026-02-28|
  assertion r.backup_purge_deadline = |2026-05-29|
```
